{"type":"standard","title":"Mark Teixeira","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mark Teixeira</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q928196","titles":{"canonical":"Mark_Teixeira","normalized":"Mark Teixeira","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mark Teixeira</span></span>"},"pageid":2071367,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Mark_Teixeira_basepaths_2011.jpg/330px-Mark_Teixeira_basepaths_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":405},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f2/Mark_Teixeira_basepaths_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2707,"height":3319},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1366013669","tid":"c9424fcf-8860-11f1-9fd6-a2a524668064","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:41:10Z","description":"American baseball player and politician (born 1980)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Teixeira","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Teixeira?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Teixeira?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mark_Teixeira"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Teixeira","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Mark_Teixeira","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Teixeira?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mark_Teixeira"}},"extract":"Mark Charles Teixeira, nicknamed \"Tex\", is an American politician and former professional baseball first baseman who played 14 seasons in Major League Baseball (MLB) for the Texas Rangers, Atlanta Braves, Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim, and New York Yankees. Before his professional career, he played college baseball at Georgia Tech, where in 2000 he won the Dick Howser Trophy as the national collegiate baseball player of the year. One of the most prolific switch hitters in MLB history, Teixeira was a member of the Yankees' 27th World Series championship team in 2009, leading the American League (AL) in home runs and runs batted in (RBI) while finishing second in the Most Valuable Player Award (MVP) balloting. Teixeira was a three-time All-Star, won five Gold Glove Awards and three Silver Slugger Awards, and holds the major-league record for most games with a home run from both sides of the plate, with 14. He was the fifth switch hitter in MLB history to reach 400 home runs.","extract_html":"<p><b>Mark Charles Teixeira</b>, nicknamed \"<b>Tex</b>\", is an American politician and former professional baseball first baseman who played 14 seasons in Major League Baseball (MLB) for the Texas Rangers, Atlanta Braves, Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim, and New York Yankees. Before his professional career, he played college baseball at Georgia Tech, where in 2000 he won the Dick Howser Trophy as the national collegiate baseball player of the year. One of the most prolific switch hitters in MLB history, Teixeira was a member of the Yankees' 27th World Series championship team in 2009, leading the American League (AL) in home runs and runs batted in (RBI) while finishing second in the Most Valuable Player Award (MVP) balloting. Teixeira was a three-time All-Star, won five Gold Glove Awards and three Silver Slugger Awards, and holds the major-league record for most games with a home run from both sides of the plate, with 14. He was the fifth switch hitter in MLB history to reach 400 home runs.</p>"}